#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: callout"
msgstr ""

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`div[class~=\"instui-callout\"]` — Inline information alert for a short reminder or note."
msgstr "`div[class~=\"instui-callout\"]` — Inline informasjonsvarsel for ei kort påminning eller merknad."

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "✅ Use Callout when:"
msgstr "✅ Bruk Callout når:"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- You need to highlight important information or reminders inline\n- The message is relatively brief (a sentence to a short paragraph)\n- The alert should draw attention without interrupting the main flow\n🚫 Don't use Callout when:"
msgstr "- Du treng å framheve viktig informasjon eller påminningar inline\n- Meldinga er relativt kort (ei setning til eit kort avsnitt)\n- Varslet bør fange merksemda utan å avbryte hovudflyten\n🚫 Ikkje bruk Callout når:"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- The message requires interaction or multiple actions — use a Modal or Alert Dialog\n- The content is the main focus of the page — use a Card or Hero layout instead"
msgstr "- Meldinga krev interaksjon eller fleire handlingar — bruk ein Modal eller Alert Dialog\n- Innhaldet er hovudfokuset på sida — bruk heller eit Card- eller Hero-oppsett"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Ensure the alert role is properly applied (role=\"alert\" or role=\"status\")\n- Use semantic color contrast that meets WCAG AA standards\n- Don't rely on color alone to convey meaning"
msgstr "- Sørg for at alert-rollen er brukt riktig (role=\"alert\" eller role=\"status\")\n- Bruk semantisk fargekontrast som oppfyller WCAG AA-standarden\n- Ikkje stol på farge åleine for å formidle meining"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Alert message content"
msgstr "Innhald i varselmeldinga"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container for the text content."
msgstr "Behaldar for tekstinnhaldet."

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Optional icon to the left of the content."
msgstr "Valfritt ikon til venstre for innhaldet."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: card"
msgstr ""

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-card` — A surface container that accepts arbitrary content."
msgstr "`.instui-card` — Ein overflatebehaldar som tek imot vilkårleg innhald."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Variant** controls how direct children are styled: `content` (default) leaves them\n  unstyled; `container` stacks them as bordered, padded sections. Padding scales with\n  viewport width and is the same across both variants.\n  **Size** is fully responsive — padding and border-radius step up automatically at 320px\n  (20rem) and 640px (40rem) via standard `min-width` media queries; no size class is needed.\n  Pair with `@pantoken/components` for heading, button, and other inline components."
msgstr "**Variant** styrer korleis direkte born blir stilsette: `content` (standard) let dei stå uformaterte; `container` stabler dei som avgrensa, polstra seksjonar. Polstringa skalerer med visningsvindauget sin breidde og er den same for begge variantar.\n  **Size** er heilt responsiv — polstring og border-radius aukar automatisk ved 320px\n  (20rem) og 640px (40rem) via standard `min-width` media queries; ingen storleiksklasse er naudsynt.\n  Pair with `@pantoken/components` for heading, button, and other inline components."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Use `<article>` as the card element when the card is a self-contained unit of content;\n  use `<section>` when grouped within a larger landmark. In `-variant-container`, prefer\n  `<section>` elements as direct children so each bordered region carries semantic meaning."
msgstr "Bruk `<article>` som kort-element når kortet er ein sjølvstendig innhaldsenhet;\n  bruk `<section>` når det er gruppert innanfor eit større landemerke. I `-variant-container`, føretrekk `<section>`-element som direkte born slik at kvar avgrensa region får semantisk meining."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Content card -nocard"
msgstr "Innhaldskort -nocard"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container card -nocard"
msgstr "Containerkort -nocard"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container card; direct children become bordered, padded sections."
msgstr "Containerkort; direkte born blir avgrensa, polstra seksjonar."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Standard content card; children are unstyled. Default when no variant is set."
msgstr "Standard innhaldskort; born er uformaterte. Standard når ingen variant er sett."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- `@scope` is Baseline 2023 Newly Available; the card degrades to an unscoped flat stylesheet\n  in older browsers with no loss of visible styling."
msgstr "- `@scope` er Baseline 2023 Newly Available; kortet fell tilbake til eit uskopa, flatt stilark i eldre nettlesarar utan tap av synleg styling."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [heading](/api/css/heading.md) — Place directly in the card or inside a container section.\n- [button](/api/css/button.md) — Place directly in the card or inside a container section.\n- [img](/api/css/img.md) — Place directly in the card as a media region.\n- [badge](/api/css/badge.md) — Place directly in the card as a status indicator."
msgstr "- [heading](/api/css/heading.md) — Plasser direkte i kortet eller inne i ein containerseksjon.\n- [button](/api/css/button.md) — Plasser direkte i kortet eller inne i ein containerseksjon.\n- [img](/api/css/img.md) — Plasser direkte i kortet som ein medieregion.\n- [badge](/api/css/badge.md) — Plasser direkte i kortet som ein statusindikator."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scoping"
msgstr "- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scoping"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: checkbox"
msgstr ""

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-checkbox` — A native checkbox and its label, or a switch via `-variant-toggle`."
msgstr "`.instui-checkbox` — ein native avkryssingsboks og etiketten hennar, eller ein brytar via `-variant-toggle`."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Set `el.indeterminate = true` in JavaScript to show the mixed-state dash; the checked tick auto-contrasts against the fill — white on a dark fill, near-black on a light one. Also sets its own `gap` between the control and its label; chaining a `-gap-*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value."
msgstr "Set `el.indeterminate = true` i JavaScript for å vise det blandede tilstandsstreken; den haketeikna for kryssa kontrasterer automatisk mot fyllfargen — kvit på mørk fyll, nesten svart på lys fyll. Set òg si eiga `gap` mellom kontrollen og etiketten; å kople på ein `-gap-*` spacing-utility-modifikator overkøyrer den innebygde verdien."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [checkbox.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/checkbox/checkbox.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [checkbox.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/checkbox/checkbox.css)"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A native `<input type=\"checkbox\">` drives `:checked`, `:indeterminate`, and `:disabled`; set `el.indeterminate = true` in JavaScript for the mixed state, and note that `-readonly` is styling only since checkboxes have no native readonly attribute."
msgstr "Ein native `<input type=\"checkbox\">` styrer `:checked`, `:indeterminate`, og `:disabled`; set `el.indeterminate = true` i JavaScript for den indeterminate tilstanden, og merk at `-readonly` berre er styling sidan avkryssingsbokser ikkje har eit native readonly-attributt."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Invalid (error) state."
msgstr "Ugyldig (feil) tilstand."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label after the control."
msgstr "Plasser etiketten etter kontrollen."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label before the control."
msgstr "Plasser etiketten før kontrollen."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label above the control."
msgstr "Plasser etiketten over kontrollen."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Read-only state."
msgstr "Skriv-bare tilstand (read-only)."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Show the required-field asterisk next to the label."
msgstr "Vis stjerna for obligatorisk felt ved sida av etiketten."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render as a switch instead of a box."
msgstr "Render som ein brytar i staden for ei boks."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The required-field asterisk."
msgstr "Stjerna for obligatorisk felt."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "On `-variant-toggle`, the state glyph riding the handle: an X when off, a check when on."
msgstr "På `-variant-toggle`, tilstandsikonet på handtaket: ein X når av, ein hake når på."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The masked tick or dash glyph centered in the box; on `-variant-toggle` it becomes the sliding handle instead."
msgstr "Det maskerte hake- eller strekteiknet midt i boksen; på `-variant-toggle` blir det i staden det glidande handtaket."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The box's mask glyph: a tick when checked, a dash when indeterminate."
msgstr "Boksens maskerte teikn: ein hake når kryssa, ein strek når indeterminate."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle border width."
msgstr "Bredda på grensa til brytaren."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle switch height."
msgstr "Høgda på brytarskinna."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The computed handle diameter."
msgstr "Utrekna diametern på handtaket."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The handle inset from each track edge."
msgstr "Innrykket til handtaket frå kvar kant av skinna."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle track width."
msgstr "Breidden på brytarskinna."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [radio](/api/css/radio.md) — The single-select counterpart."
msgstr "- [radio](/api/css/radio.md) — Den einskilde valmotparten."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: close-button"
msgstr ""

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-close-button` — A transparent icon button that draws its own × glyph, in three sizes plus an on-color variant."
msgstr "`.instui-close-button` — Ein gjennomsiktig ikonknapp som teiknar sitt eige ×-teikn, i tre storleikar pluss ein variant for fargebakgrunn."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Always renders as an icon-only control with no visible label, so an `aria-label` is required, not optional; compare to `button`'s `-without-background` ghost variant, which keeps a text label."
msgstr "Visast alltid som ein ikon-berre kontroll utan synleg etikett, så ein `aria-label` er påkravd, ikkje valfri; samanlikn med `button` sin `-without-background` \"ghost\"-variant, som beheld ein tekstetikett."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [close-button.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/close-button/close-button.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [close-button.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/close-button/close-button.css)"

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Give the icon-only button an `aria-label` (e.g. \"Close\"), and mark a disabled button with `aria-disabled` (or the native `disabled`)."
msgstr "Gje ikon-berre knappen ein `aria-label` (t.d. \"Close\"), og marker ein deaktivert knapp med `aria-disabled` (eller den native `disabled`)."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "For a close button placed on a coloured (non-neutral) surface."
msgstr "For ein lukkeknapp plassert på ein farga (ikkje-nøytral) flate."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The × glyph, masked in `currentColor`."
msgstr "×-teiknet, maskert i `currentColor`."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [button](/api/css/button.md) — The general-purpose action button."
msgstr "- [button](/api/css/button.md) — Den generelle handlingsknappen."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: color"
msgstr ""

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.--text-danger` — Semantic colour utilities: `.--bg-<name>`, `.--text-<name>` (aliased as `.--color-<name>`), and `.--border-<name>` for the curated semantic palette. Every one of these also has a component-attached alias modifier (for example `-bg-danger` on any `.instui-<component>`)."
msgstr "`.--text-danger` — Semantiske fargeverktøy: `.--bg-<name>`, `.--text-<name>` (aliasert som `.--color-<name>`), og `.--border-<name>` for den kuraterte semantiske paletten. Kvar av desse har òg ein komponent-tilknytt alias-modifikator (til dømes `-bg-danger` på eit vilkårleg `.instui-<component>`)."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [generate.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/scripts/generate.ts)"
msgstr "**Source:** [generate.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/scripts/generate.ts)"

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Applies the semantic danger text colour."
msgstr "Gjev den semantiske fare-tekstfargen."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Background colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "Bakgrunnsfargeverktøy for semantiske og komponent-tilpassa namn."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Border colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "Rammefargeverktøy for semantiske og komponent-tilpassa namn."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Alias of `--text-*` for text colour utilities."
msgstr "Alias for `--text-*` for tekstfargeverktøy."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Text colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "Tekstfargeverktøy for semantiske og komponent-tilpassa namn."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: context-view"
msgstr ""

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-context-view` — An elevated callout with a caret, positionable on any side; works as a native `[popover]`."
msgstr "`.instui-context-view` — Ein opphøgd merknad med ein pekar, kan posisjonast på alle sider; fungerer som ein innfødd `[popover]`."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The caret is two stacked `::before`/`::after` triangles (border then fill) so it reads correctly against a matching surface; as a `[popover]` it needs the same open/`popovertarget` wiring as `popover`, but unlike `tooltip`, it dismisses on outside click or Escape."
msgstr "Pekaren er to stablede `::before`/`::after`-trekantar (ramme og fyll) slik at han lesast korrekt mot ei matchande flate; som ein `[popover]` treng han same open/`popovertarget`-kopling som `popover`, men i motsetnad til `tooltip` blir han avvist ved klikk utanfor eller ved Escape."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [context-view.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/context-view/context-view.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [context-view.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/context-view/context-view.css)"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Dark (inverse) colour scheme."
msgstr "Mørkt (invertert) fargesett."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit below the anchor."
msgstr "Plasser under ankret."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit at the end (inline-end) of the anchor."
msgstr "Plasser ved enden (inline-end) av ankret."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit at the start (inline-start) of the anchor."
msgstr "Plasser ved starten (inline-start) av ankret."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit above the anchor."
msgstr "Plasser over ankret."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the caret's inner fill triangle."
msgstr "Gjer render av pekarens indre fylte trekant."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the caret's outer border triangle."
msgstr "Gjer render av pekarens ytre kant-trekant."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Uses CSS anchor positioning (`position-anchor`, `position-area`, `position-try-fallbacks`) and the native `[popover]` API behind an `@supports` guard; needs a recent Chromium or Safari, and falls back to a UA-centred popover elsewhere."
msgstr "- Brukar CSS-anchor-posisjonering (`position-anchor`, `position-area`, `position-try-fallbacks`) og den native `[popover]`-API-en bak ei `@supports`-vern; krev ein nyare Chromium eller Safari, og fell tilbake til ein UA-sentrert popover andre stader."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [popover](/api/css/popover.md) — The generic top-layer popover.\n- [tooltip](/api/css/tooltip.md) — A smaller hover or focus callout."
msgstr "- [popover](/api/css/popover.md) — Den generiske topplags-popoveren.\n- [tooltip](/api/css/tooltip.md) — Ein mindre vising ved hovring eller fokus."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: cursor"
msgstr ""

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.--cursor-pointer` — `cursor` as a composable, global class — `.--cursor-<value>` — usable bare or chained onto any component (`.instui-button.--cursor-pointer`)."
msgstr "`.--cursor-pointer` — `cursor` som ei komponerbar, global klasse — `.--cursor-<value>` — kan brukast åleine eller koplast til ein kvar komponent (`.instui-button.--cursor-pointer`)."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
