msgstr "Katalansk (Catalá) lokalisasjonspakke."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Variable: calendar"
msgstr "# Variabel: calendar"

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-calendar>` — an interactive month grid. `value` (`yyyy-mm-dd`) is the selected day and\n`view` (`yyyy-mm-dd`, optional) the visible month. The prev/next chevrons and every day are\n`<button>`s driving the Invoker Commands API (`--calendar-prev`, `--calendar-next`,\n`--calendar-select`) at the grid; selecting a day updates `value`/`view` and dispatches a composed,\nbubbling `change` event (`detail.value` is the ISO date). Renders its own grid (no slot), so it\nworks standalone or nested inside a date picker."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-calendar&gt;` — an interactive month grid. `value` (`yyyy-mm-dd`) is the selected day and\n`view` (`yyyy-mm-dd`, optional) the visible month. The prev/next chevrons and every day are\n`&lt;button&gt;`s driving the Invoker Commands API (`--calendar-prev`, `--calendar-next`,\n`--calendar-select`) at the grid; selecting a day updates `value`/`view` and dispatches a composed,\nbubbling `change` event (`detail.value` is the ISO date). Renders its own grid (no slot), so it\nworks standalone or nested inside a date picker."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/contextView.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Variable: contextView"
msgstr "# Variabel: contextView"

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/contextView.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-context-view>` — a callout surface with a caret. The host itself is a native `[popover]`\n(top layer + light-dismiss), so a light-DOM `popovertarget`/`command` button can toggle it by id.\nPosition it near its trigger with CSS anchor positioning where supported; otherwise it centres in\nthe top layer. Content goes in the default slot."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-context-view&gt;` — a callout surface with a caret. The host itself is a native `[popover]`\n(top layer + light-dismiss), so a light-DOM `popovertarget`/`command` button can toggle it by id.\nPosition it near its trigger with CSS anchor positioning where supported; otherwise it centres in\nthe top layer. Content goes in the default slot."

